	index, and the question that comes up most -- which font mechanism for
	non-Latin-1 text -- is answered at the top with the measured sizes.
	* tests/new-0.9.4.16.test: the aes256 constraint measures instead of
	being hard-coded to 0. It wrote one encrypted file and timed it;
	under the threshold the fourteen tests run, over it they are skipped
	and the message names the figure, the threshold and the backend.
	Whether AES-256 is too slow depends on the machine: algorithm 2.B runs
	at least 64 rounds, each encrypting some 3.4 kB with AES-CBC -- about
	216 kB in pure Tcl. Not the hashing: 64 SHA-384 over 3 kB take one
	millisecond, and the C-based tcl-sha backend brings 22.4 s down to
	only 20.5. AES-128 takes 157 ms by comparison.
	* tests/init.tcl: the test tree is located by searching upwards for
	pkgIndex.tcl next to src/, not by taking [file join [pwd] ..]. That
	pointed one level above the WORKING directory rather than above the
	test file, so "tclsh tests/font.test" from the root looked for
	../examples outside the tree: seven tests skipped and font-6.1 failing
	with a message about getFonts for what was a path error. 38 uses of
	../examples across eight files now go through $::pdf4tclTestRoot.
	* tests/font.test: font-6.1 asks for MyArial, which font-4.1 and
	font-5.1 register, and carried no constraint -- on a machine with
	neither face it failed rather than being skipped. font-7.1 and 7.2
	pin that the root is found and carries the example fonts.
	* src/main.tcl: /Producer is filled in where the caller left it. ISO
	19005-3 table 7 pairs it with pdf:Producer, which pdf4tcl writes
	unasked, so the two sides of the crosswalk disagreed -- XMP named the
	release, /Info named nothing. Clause 6.6.3 puts this as a should, so
	no file was ever invalid for it; it was inconsistent. -producer still
	overrides, on both sides.
	* tests/pdfa.test: 4 tests covering all eight pairs of table 7, 92 in
	total.
	* src/main.tcl (addEmbeddedFile): /AFRelationship defaults to
	Unspecified instead of being left out. ISO 19005-3 clause 6.8 refers
	to annex E: an embedded file meeting the extra requirements is an
	associated file and needs one. Measured: without it veraPDF fails the
	document at clause 6.8 -- a PDF/A-3 file that was not one. facturx
	set it already; a plain attachment did not.
	* tests/pdfa.test: 3 tests, 88 in total.
	* src/options.tcl, src/main.tcl: -pdfa accepts 2u and 3u, and the XMP
	says U. ISO 19005-2 clause 5.4: a level U file skips only the
	requirements of clause 6.7, where a level B file also skips 6.2.11.7 --
	so U is B plus the Unicode mappings, which pdf4tcl writes anyway.
	Measured: veraPDF accepts both. There is no 1u; the level came in with
	part 2 (clause 5.4 note 3).
	* tests/pdfa.test: 5 tests, 85 in total.
